<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-trigonometry-ii" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Trigonometry II</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
        In this chapter, we will build on the concepts of trigonometry that we learned earlier.
    </p>
    <p>
        We will explore how to extend our understanding of trigonometric ratios to angles beyond acute angles, and how to apply these concepts to solve more complex problems.
    </p>
    <p>
        Additionally, we will also delve into the unit circle, radians, and graphing trigonometric functions.
    </p>
    <p>
        By the end of this chapter, you will have a deeper understanding of trigonometry and its applications in real life.
    </p>
  </introduction>

